{"units": [{"id": "mvp-comment-146-1-mentioned5", "translation": "to attain, to light upon"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-146-1-mentioned6", "translation": "they attained"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-146-1-mentioned7", "translation": "l"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-146-1-mentioned8", "translation": "to every"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-146-1-mentioned9", "translation": "to a torch"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-146-1-mentioned10", "translation": "hard to traverse, rugged"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-146-1-mentioned11", "translation": "even beneath the earth"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-146-1-mentioned12", "translation": "not to be persuaded, implacable"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-146-1-mentioned13", "translation": "hard to traverse"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-146-1-mentioned14", "translation": "immortal"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-146-1-mentioned15", "translation": "unwearied"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-146-1-mentioned16", "translation": "a shield-bearing armed company"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-146-1-mentioned17", "translation": "through the house and city of Oedipus"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-146-1-mentioned18", "translation": "holding a position"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-146-1-mentioned19", "translation": "and"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-146-1-mentioned20", "translation": "and there is for me an ancient privilege"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-146-1-mentioned21", "translation": "is"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-146-1-mentioned22", "translation": "and not to attain dishonor, even beneath the earth, holding a position"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-146-2-comment1", "translation": "⟦1⟧ is rightly compared with ⟦2⟧: ⟦3⟧; only here the subject is developed in a separate new clause: ⟦4⟧."}, {"id": "mvp-comment-146-2-mentioned1", "translation": "for it remains"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-146-2-mentioned2", "translation": "but it remains, while Zeus remains on his throne, that the doer suffer"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-146-2-mentioned3", "translation": "and resourceful and..."}, {"id": "mvp-comment-146-3-comment1", "translation": "⟦1⟧ as in the antistrophe; thus ⟦2⟧ (Wakefield) instead of the manuscripts' ⟦3⟧ seems assured. But the new clause would need a finite verb, even if ⟦4⟧ could possibly be supplied; moreover, ⟦5⟧ (= ⟦6⟧) ⟦7⟧ cannot be exactly paralleled, although ⟦8⟧ \"to pursue\" (⟦9⟧ schol.) is common in Attic poetry. Therefore with Heath ⟦10⟧, cf. 931. ⟦11⟧; ⟦12⟧ may have been repeated thoughtlessly after v. 358. Weil, however, takes a different view: ⟦13⟧ (thus -⟦14⟧ M, and so also the schol.), with slight transposition and minor change. But neither is anything like ⟦15⟧ attested, nor is ⟦16⟧ correct: ⟦17⟧ it says later."}, {"id": "mvp-comment-146-3-mentioned1", "translation": "and"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-146-3-mentioned2", "translation": "and"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-146-3-mentioned3", "translation": "but"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-146-3-mentioned4", "translation": "we are"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-146-3-mentioned5", "translation": "pursuing"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-146-3-mentioned6", "translation": "pursuing"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-146-3-mentioned7", "translation": "allotments, privileges"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-146-3-mentioned8", "translation": "to pursue"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-146-3-mentioned9", "translation": "going after, pursuing"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-146-3-mentioned10", "translation": "we manage, we administer"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-146-3-mentioned11", "translation": "pursuing"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-146-3-mentioned12", "translation": "we honor the unhonored; it is unhonored"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-146-3-mentioned13", "translation": "tai"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-146-3-mentioned14", "translation": "to honor; allotments"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-146-3-mentioned15", "translation": "it is unhonored"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-146-3-mentioned16", "translation": "and I do not attain dishonor"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-146-4-comment1", "translation": "⟦1⟧ of two endings, like ⟦2⟧. Frg. 11, 7, but mostly of three, as at v. 214. ⟦3⟧ ⟦4⟧;"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-146-4-mentioned1", "translation": "perfect, fulfilled"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-146-4-mentioned2", "translation": "mindful Erinyes"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-146-5-comment1", "translation": "⟦1⟧ is the Athenian cult name of the Eumenides, Preller-Robert Myth. 838; also below at 1041. Heimsoeth and Paley therefore capitalize it; for if it were simply an adjective, the word would have to be joined with ⟦2⟧, which is not a good combination and also gives an unpleasant enjambment."}, {"id": "mvp-comment-146-5-mentioned1", "translation": "the August, the Revered"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-146-5-mentioned2", "translation": "and hard to appease for mortals"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-146-6-comment1", "translation": "⟦1⟧ with the same litotes as ⟦2⟧ ⟦3⟧; but see also 387 ⟦4⟧, 396 ⟦5⟧ = ⟦6⟧ 387, 388 ⟦7⟧, in which accumulation there is a certain intention to emphasize the repulsive."}, {"id": "mvp-comment-146-6-mentioned1", "translation": "hard to appease"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-146-6-mentioned2", "translation": "hard to traverse, rugged"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-146-6-mentioned3", "translation": "sunless"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-146-6-mentioned4", "translation": "sunless"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-146-6-mentioned5", "translation": "with terrible eyes"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-146-6-quote1", "translation": "hard to entreat, inexorable"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-146-7-comment1", "translation": "⟦1⟧ (cf. ⟦2⟧, ⟦3⟧, ⟦4⟧ etc.) also at 839. ⟦5⟧."}, {"id": "mvp-comment-146-7-mentioned1", "translation": "unhonored"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-146-7-mentioned2", "translation": "unlit"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-146-7-mentioned3", "translation": "unconquerable"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-146-7-mentioned4", "translation": "abominable"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-146-8-comment1", "translation": "⟦1⟧ (⟦2⟧) is the same as ⟦3⟧. 360 ff. The transmitted ⟦4⟧ Dindorf corrects to ⟦5⟧, likewise 396 ⟦6⟧ to ⟦7⟧; in this strophic pair the Attic forms are almost throughout in the manuscripts, unlike in the other strophes, but at least in this verse ⟦8⟧."}, {"id": "mvp-comment-146-8-mentioned1", "translation": "the gods being divided"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-146-8-mentioned2", "translation": "and to keep away from the immortals..."}, {"id": "mvp-comment-146-8-mentioned3", "translation": "sunless"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-146-8-mentioned4", "translation": "sunless"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-146-8-mentioned5", "translation": "sunless"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-146-8-mentioned6", "translation": "sunless"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-146-8-mentioned7", "translation": "to a torch"}]}